WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:32.490
Admiral Kizaru
has made landfall!

3
00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.650
The battle has begun!

4
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.940
Don't let them
fire those lasers!

5
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:38.240
Attack!

6
00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:20.900
Damn!

7
00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.880
<b>Sentomaru</b>

8
00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:29.080
Those boxes are closing
in from all sides!

9
00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:29.910
What do we do?

10
00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:30.780
Just shoot!

11
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:33.050
We'll get them before
they can get us!

12
00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:44.770
Stand back!

13
00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.090
I got this one!

14
00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:50.420
Steam Knuckles!

15
00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:10.700
You wanna destroy
those ships?

16
00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.620
You're gonna have
to go through me!

17
00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:20.130
All the Vice-Admirals
have landed!

18
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.430
So where's the lab where they're
holding the Cipher Pol agents?

19
00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:33.230
Way up top.

20
00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:34.030
Hmm?

21
00:03:38.240 --> 00:03:40.120
<b>In the Labophase...</b>

22
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.750
The Navy and the robot
sea beasts are fighting!

23
00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.080
Oh man, looks like
they're going all out!

24
00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:47.580
They should be safe for now.

25
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:53.050
<b>Pacifista
Authority
Hierarchy</b>
<b>Five Elders</b>
<b>Vegapunk
(Stella + Satellites)</b>
<b>Authority Chip</b>

26
00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:46.370
<b>Sentomaru Authority Chip</b>

27
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:53.050
<b>Sentomaru</b>

28
00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:46.580
<b>Vegapunk
(Stella + Satellites) Pacifista
Authority
Hierarchy</b>
<b>Vegapunk
(Stella + Satellites) Authority Chip</b>

29
00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:46.660
<b>Five Elders Pacifista
Authority
Hierarchy</b>

30
00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:50.630
Sentomaru is still
in command of our pacifistas.

31
00:03:50.710 --> 00:03:53.130
Our defenses
remain iron-tight.

32
00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:54.670
And they know that!

33
00:03:54.750 --> 00:03:58.100
Which is the whole reason they
sent him after Sentomaru!

34
00:03:58.180 --> 00:03:58.980
Kizaru?

35
00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:01.110
He's on this shore already?

36
00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:02.020
Oh no!

37
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.120
Closer!

38
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:05.800
He's fighting right below us!

39
00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.160
Kizaru's here?

40
00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:11.530
This brings back some unpleasant
memories from our first trip to Sabaody.

41
00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.640
Well, you're screwed.

42
00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:21.640
Sucks to be you.

43
00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:24.100
Why does he have to fight
Kizaru, of all people?

44
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:26.400
I'm sorry, Sentomaru!

45
00:04:26.480 --> 00:04:28.570
I won't blame you if you
choose to run away!

46
00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:29.730
What a gruesome affair!

47
00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:32.120
It's gonna be okay, Stella!

48
00:04:32.590 --> 00:04:34.420
We don't have time
to worry right now!

49
00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:35.830
Just focus
on cracking the code!

50
00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:39.220
We've got a job!

51
00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.210
Michelle!

52
00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:48.530
I really would hate
to hurt you, friend.

53
00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.280
Why don't you
surrender for me?

54
00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.020
Sacred Yasakani Jewel!

55
00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:14.010
I'm not happy
about this myself!

56
00:05:14.090 --> 00:05:15.630
But I made a promise!

57
00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.650
A deal with Straw Hat Luffy!

58
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:20.230
With Straw Hat?

59
00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:23.920
Since when are you the kind of man
who makes deals with pirates?

60
00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:34.390
I'll take any ally I can get!

61
00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.920
To get him out of here!

62
00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:41.150
I will let him die!

63
00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:42.480
I will!

64
00:06:00.910 --> 00:06:01.810
Oh...

65
00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:02.720
Huh?

66
00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.670
Hm?!

67
00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.840
Well, ain't that a surprise!

68
00:06:10.270 --> 00:06:13.470
Looks like our gang of bears
has already been taken care of.

69
00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:15.720
Did that child beat
them on his own?

70
00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:16.930
No.

71
00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:21.200
I lived in the village,
but I won't go back there.

72
00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.340
The people are all
weak and stupid.

73
00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:24.680
I see.

74
00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.340
So they kicked you out, huh?

75
00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.360
I'm strong enough
to wrestle bears.

76
00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.570
I don't get tired or hungry,
but I need a job.

77
00:06:32.650 --> 00:06:33.670
And I need money.

78
00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:37.730
Oh, is there something
important you need to buy?

79
00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:39.670
Yes, rice balls.

80
00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.700
You were so
adorable back then.

81
00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.410
So, you need a job.

82
00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:58.470
You've proven your strength.

83
00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.470
I could put that to good use.

84
00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.980
Well, boy, what would you say
to becoming my bodyguard?

85
00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.790
You really want to hire me?

86
00:07:05.870 --> 00:07:06.690
Yes!

87
00:07:06.770 --> 00:07:07.640
I'll do it!

88
00:07:12.940 --> 00:07:13.770
Uncle!

89
00:07:14.980 --> 00:07:15.810
Uncle!

90
00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.100
Huh?

91
00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:18.150
What?

92
00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.480
Are you talking to me?

93
00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:20.640
Help me, Uncle.

94
00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.510
I've never been a bodyguard.

95
00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:24.130
How should I keep on safe?

96
00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:25.980
Kid, I am not your uncle.

97
00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.780
Well, at least you're
not calling me Gramps.

98
00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:30.610
Teach me everything
you know.

99
00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:31.700
I'll train hard!

100
00:07:35.810 --> 00:07:38.640
I tried my best to teach
you, Sentomaru.

101
00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.740
I really did.

102
00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:41.880
Sumo Strike!

103
00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:47.740
But you forget.

104
00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:52.570
For as much as you brag
about your defense...

105
00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.200
...mine is just as good.

106
00:08:24.180 --> 00:08:25.510
Come in, pacifistas.

107
00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.120
Your previous commander
is currently unconscious.

108
00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.060
And your mission
has changed.

109
00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:38.730
You will provide support to the Navy
fleet surrounding Egghead.

110
00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.650
Sink the Sea Beast weapons!

111
00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.590
We command
the pacifistas now.

112
00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:11.740
Their order was revised.

113
00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.900
Quite the waste to sink
those sea beasts.

114
00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:17.710
But far better to save
the pacifistas.

115
00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:20.690
Seems there's been
sizable damage.

116
00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:22.330
Give me a report.

117
00:09:22.410 --> 00:09:23.240
Yes, sir.

118
00:09:26.650 --> 00:09:28.600
Kizaru just took
out Sentomaru!

119
00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:29.510
He burns!

120
00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.660
We need to shut down
this defense system immediately!

121
00:09:41.740 --> 00:09:42.440
Roger!

122
00:09:42.850 --> 00:09:45.500
We can't let Sentomaru's
efforts go to waste!

123
00:09:45.990 --> 00:09:47.450
He bought us his time!

124
00:09:47.530 --> 00:09:48.820
He'll never crack it!

125
00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.530
Trust me, I'm Dr. Vegapunk.

126
00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:51.440
Heard of me?

127
00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.800
Kizaru is light itself.

128
00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:00.370
He can get past the laser
barrier in an instant.

129
00:10:04.820 --> 00:10:05.620
What?!

130
00:10:06.070 --> 00:10:08.540
You mean we got no
defenses against this guy?

131
00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:09.820
Precisely.

132
00:10:09.900 --> 00:10:10.720
Ha ha ha!

133
00:10:10.800 --> 00:10:12.740
I can't... I can't... I can't...

134
00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.200
What the hell are we
supposed to do now?

135
00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:17.990
He kicked our butts when
we fought him before!

136
00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:23.810
Looks like we
get a round two.

137
00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:26.370
Let's see how long
your strides last.

138
00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:45.010
Give it some hustle, yeah?

139
00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:48.080
As soon as that barrier comes
down, this ship's gotta fly!

140
00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.140
We're doing great,
don't you worry!

141
00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:53.740
I'll have everything
in position in no time!

142
00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:55.410
We're counting on you!

143
00:11:00.550 --> 00:11:03.020
We'd better eat while
we still can, Luffy!

144
00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.240
Good point.

145
00:11:09.720 --> 00:11:12.210
Can't fight on an empty
stomach, I say.

146
00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:12.860
Hey!

147
00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.500
Could you two try to focus?

148
00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:17.640
Don't stuff your faces when
we're about to blast off!

149
00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:19.810
Uh-oh.

150
00:11:23.050 --> 00:11:23.890
Hey, Lilith!

151
00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.030
What's that alarm?

152
00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.940
It sounds like somebody broke
in, but I don't know how.

153
00:11:29.300 --> 00:11:31.210
Who could get
through the barrier?

154
00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:33.230
It's supposed to be
impenetrable!

155
00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:49.000
They gave me a checklist
of things I shouldn't destroy.

156
00:11:49.770 --> 00:11:51.830
First off is the power plant.

157
00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.400
Followed by Punk Records.

158
00:11:56.400 --> 00:11:57.300
And York.

159
00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:04.920
It's a real pity that my dear old
friend didn't make the list this time.

160
00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:09.520
The list of what I have
to destroy is shorter.

161
00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:12.260
Just one man.

162
00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.180
Doctor Vegapunk.

163
00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:16.760
The barrier was useless!

164
00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:18.490
Kizaru's inside the dome!

165
00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:21.080
Wait, wait, wait!

166
00:12:21.080 --> 00:12:22.470
Where are Luffy
and the others?

167
00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:23.600
They're stuck out
there with him!

168
00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:25.220
What do we do?

169
00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:26.260
Tell them through the snail!

170
00:12:26.260 --> 00:12:27.510
They have no idea!

171
00:12:27.590 --> 00:12:28.290
Luffy!

172
00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:30.570
Run for your life!

173
00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.050
Our plan won't succeed
unless the ship is in position.

174
00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:37.050
The barrier stays up till then.

175
00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:08.280
Stussy!

176
00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:10.100
Hey, wait!

177
00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.080
Filthy bastard!

178
00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:13.370
Let me borrow this!

179
00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.640
What the hell?!

180
00:13:16.720 --> 00:13:18.880
Why am I the one
in the damn bubble?!

181
00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:21.070
It's your partner's fault.

182
00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.160
Not mine.

183
00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:36.800
You think you own this place
because your buddy's here?

184
00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.090
You can't defeat
me and Kizaru.

185
00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.330
The noose is tightening
around your neck.

186
00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:43.590
You don't know what
we're capable of.

187
00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:12.130
I wondered why I didn't see
their ship on the shoreline.

188
00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.120
Look at you, sneaking away.

189
00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:15.540
We gotta hurry!

190
00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:18.780
Kizaru?

191
00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:20.520
A freakin' admiral?

192
00:14:20.600 --> 00:14:22.130
What's our plan, Luffy?

193
00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:24.980
Please don't tell
me he ran off!

194
00:14:25.060 --> 00:14:25.720
Hey!

195
00:14:25.720 --> 00:14:26.520
Luffy!

196
00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:40.720
Straw hat.

197
00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:41.760
Long time no...

198
00:14:51.100 --> 00:14:53.420
I see your manners
haven't improved.

199
00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:56.480
I'll warn you.

200
00:14:56.840 --> 00:14:59.100
We're not the same
as two years ago.

201
00:14:59.800 --> 00:15:01.230
We're a hundred times better.

202
00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.160
I'm stronger.

203
00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:08.640
<b>The Previous Day
Mary Geoise</b>

204
00:15:19.400 --> 00:15:21.400
The Invincible
Slave has returned!

205
00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:23.130
We don't know
what he wants!

206
00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:23.990
Be careful!

207
00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.640
Stop him, you fools!

208
00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:32.200
That monster is
destroying our city!

209
00:15:49.090 --> 00:15:50.690
We can't hold him back!

210
00:16:06.230 --> 00:16:07.640
Ursus Shock!

211
00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:17.070
Don't die!

212
00:16:26.090 --> 00:16:27.290
How dare you?!

213
00:16:27.370 --> 00:16:28.880
You're nothing but a slave!

214
00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.700
What the hell are
you trying to pull!

215
00:16:44.320 --> 00:16:47.540
The revolutionaries gave us
enough mess to clean up!

216
00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:54.860
If you got an explanation
I'd love to hear it, Kuma!

217
00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:00.660
Fleet Admiral Sakazuki...

218
00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:05.330
You're useless!

219
00:17:05.410 --> 00:17:08.230
We can't rely on you
soldiers for a thing!

220
00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:09.540
Hey!

221
00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:10.900
Speaking of which...

222
00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:12.700
Akainu!

223
00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:15.750
I wanted lobster for dinner,
but there was none to be found!

224
00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:18.850
It's an unprecedented
disaster!

225
00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:21.500
What's happening to the Holy
Land's food supply?!

226
00:17:21.580 --> 00:17:22.870
Never mind your dinner plans!

227
00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:25.590
I've been injured by
this rampaging oaf!

228
00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:29.120
A disobedient slave
must be dealt with!

229
00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:31.650
Stop fooling around
and kill him already!

230
00:17:33.260 --> 00:17:34.610
You know the deal.

231
00:17:35.340 --> 00:17:37.950
We can't let you run
around free, Kuma.

232
00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:40.140
You're too dangerous.

233
00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:43.600
Either we keep you on a leash
or we put you in the ground.

234
00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:46.210
You should have lost
all sense of identity.

235
00:17:47.450 --> 00:17:50.300
That makes you as
good as dead already.

236
00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:55.120
So what are you trying
to accomplish here?!

237
00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:06.530
Hellhound!

238
00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:06.730
<b>Hellhound</b>

239
00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.940
I didn't know you could still
bleed like a human.

240
00:18:20.540 --> 00:18:27.550
And that's what you get
for turning this into a monster!

241
00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.130
Ugh!

242
00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:02.710
You can bark all you like,
but Kuma's mind is long gone.

243
00:19:02.790 --> 00:19:04.710
He'll be reborn as a weapon.

244
00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.450
He even volunteered
for the process.

245
00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:08.900
You're a liar!

246
00:19:10.820 --> 00:19:12.530
He'd never do that.

247
00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:14.470
Not unless you forced him to!

248
00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:16.840
He wouldn't leave me!

249
00:19:16.920 --> 00:19:19.190
He wouldn't throw
his whole life away!

250
00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.280
Hey!

251
00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:27.420
Did you let Kuma escape?

252
00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.700
Why aren't you
doing your job?

253
00:19:29.780 --> 00:19:32.160
You're the fleet
admiral, aren't you?

254
00:19:35.030 --> 00:19:36.350
You're just a puppet.

255
00:19:37.060 --> 00:19:40.490
Think for yourself,
or act for yourself.

256
00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:44.790
<b>Present Day
Egghead
New World</b>

257
00:19:40.890 --> 00:19:44.490
So where the hell could you
be going on your own?

258
00:19:47.530 --> 00:19:49.500
Pacifistas and all marines!

259
00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:51.040
Continue your assault!

260
00:19:51.630 --> 00:19:53.470
Destroy every last
Sea Beast Weapon!

261
00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:54.560
Weapons!

262
00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.810
Occupy the Fabriophase!

263
00:20:08.890 --> 00:20:10.680
We're seizing the whole island!

264
00:20:10.760 --> 00:20:12.800
Admiral Kizaru is
above the clouds!

265
00:20:12.880 --> 00:20:14.770
He's just entered
the Labophase!

266
00:20:35.620 --> 00:20:36.780
Gum-Gum!

267
00:20:41.780 --> 00:20:42.900
Black Mamba!

268
00:20:49.970 --> 00:20:53.080
I see how you managed
to beat Kaido.

269
00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:54.660
You're certainly tough enough.

270
00:20:55.000 --> 00:20:56.040
But I wonder...

271
00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:01.660
What business does a pirate like
you have protecting Dr. Vegapunk?

272
00:21:01.740 --> 00:21:04.020
You're putting a lot
on the line for him.

273
00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:07.450
What business do you
have trying to kill him?

274
00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.540
Old Man Apple helped
you guys a lot.

275
00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.540
Why do you want
to get rid of it?

276
00:21:18.190 --> 00:21:19.750
It's not that I want to.

277
00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:31.270
How far up is he going?

278
00:21:40.460 --> 00:21:42.280
I'd rather not kill him at all.

279
00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:49.720
I've known Vegapunk
for a long time.

280
00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:55.400
So to be frank, I don't
need to hear your opinion.

281
00:22:00.930 --> 00:22:02.730
Acceleration is power.

282
00:22:18.150 --> 00:22:19.940
It's complete!

283
00:22:20.710 --> 00:22:23.250
It's name is Vegaforce-01!

284
00:22:24.210 --> 00:22:27.320
So dream of all mankind!

285
00:22:29.490 --> 00:22:30.860
It's a giant robot!

286
00:22:45.070 --> 00:22:46.550
Luffy!

287
00:23:11.630 --> 00:23:13.410
Thank God evil never dies.

288
00:23:23.460 --> 00:23:24.260
Lilith!

289
00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:29.390
We gotta run!

290
00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.600
The Vegaforce-01 is gonna...

291
00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:06.510
The Vegaforce-01 was
the dream of mankind!

292
00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:07.580
That's it, bro.

293
00:24:07.660 --> 00:24:08.980
You are gonna pay!

294
00:24:10.480 --> 00:24:11.880
Is the Sunny all right?

295
00:24:13.500 --> 00:24:14.330
Hold up!

296
00:24:14.410 --> 00:24:15.610
Might wanna check
on Straw Hat!

297
00:24:15.610 --> 00:24:17.080
Yeah, while you're at it!

298
00:24:25.820 --> 00:24:28.000
Kizaru, you bastard!

299
00:24:33.490 --> 00:24:36.020
Why, I hardly
recognized you, Bonney.

300
00:24:36.100 --> 00:24:37.220
My word.

301
00:24:37.640 --> 00:24:40.540
Kids these days
grow up real fast.

302
00:24:43.740 --> 00:24:45.450
So what's your stake in this?

303
00:24:45.850 --> 00:24:48.950
Did you want to take revenge
on Vegapunk yourself?

304
00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:52.210
Are you mad we're gonna
beat you to the punch?

305
00:24:54.020 --> 00:24:54.820
Shut up!

306
00:24:56.340 --> 00:24:59.280
Vegapunk isn't the one
I'm trying to kill anymore.

307
00:25:03.340 --> 00:25:04.530
Age Skewer!

308
00:25:06.070 --> 00:25:06.870
Oh, my.

309
00:25:11.910 --> 00:25:13.700
You're not part of my mission.

310
00:25:14.980 --> 00:25:19.320
So don't make me shoot down
another acquaintance, please.

311
00:25:20.740 --> 00:25:21.540
No!

312
00:25:22.960 --> 00:25:24.080
The barrier!

313
00:25:24.800 --> 00:25:25.630
Bonney!

314
00:25:32.150 --> 00:25:33.610
Enough, Kizaru!

315
00:25:33.690 --> 00:25:34.630
You're done for!

316
00:25:37.050 --> 00:25:38.130
Radical!

317
00:25:43.500 --> 00:25:47.080
Wait... He's gone?

318
00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:48.220
Kizaru!

319
00:25:48.670 --> 00:25:49.660
Where'd he go?

320
00:25:50.240 --> 00:25:51.420
Stella's in danger.

321
00:25:51.770 --> 00:25:53.540
Franky, call the control room!

322
00:25:54.120 --> 00:25:57.330
<b>Control Room
Labophase</b>

323
00:26:00.230 --> 00:26:01.550
Yo, control room!

324
00:26:01.630 --> 00:26:02.410
Hey, Franky!

325
00:26:02.490 --> 00:26:03.320
You okay?

326
00:26:03.400 --> 00:26:05.680
I just heard a big
explosion over there!

327
00:26:05.760 --> 00:26:06.680
Never mind me.

328
00:26:06.760 --> 00:26:07.820
Are you guys safe?

329
00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:09.550
Yeah?

330
00:26:09.550 --> 00:26:10.450
Why?

331
00:26:10.530 --> 00:26:12.500
Oh, guess he's not there yet.

332
00:26:12.580 --> 00:26:13.670
Lucky break.

333
00:26:13.750 --> 00:26:15.490
You are making me nervous.

334
00:26:15.940 --> 00:26:17.310
It is done!

335
00:26:17.740 --> 00:26:20.660
That puny encryption
was no match for us.

336
00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:23.460
We're free!

337
00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:26.260
Nice work!

338
00:26:28.660 --> 00:26:30.760
Eat that, York!

339
00:26:30.840 --> 00:26:31.540
You lose!

340
00:26:32.380 --> 00:26:35.320
You stupid pumpkin geniuses!

341
00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:37.450
Hello, Franky.

342
00:26:37.530 --> 00:26:40.060
We can deactivate
the barrier any time you like.

343
00:26:40.140 --> 00:26:43.230
Did you move the Vegaforce-01
and the ship to the back side yet?

344
00:26:43.230 --> 00:26:43.930
Not yet.

345
00:26:43.980 --> 00:26:44.980
It's complicated.

346
00:26:48.000 --> 00:26:53.410
Hate to be the bearer of bad news,
but your escape plan is a bust.

347
00:26:56.520 --> 00:26:58.030
Hello, old friend.

348
00:27:05.020 --> 00:27:06.720
When did you get here?

349
00:27:07.160 --> 00:27:07.940
Wait!

350
00:27:08.020 --> 00:27:09.670
So what did you do to Luffy?

351
00:27:09.750 --> 00:27:11.360
You didn't kill him, did you?

352
00:27:11.440 --> 00:27:12.860
They're so... dead.

353
00:27:14.280 --> 00:27:16.920
Are you the cause
of that explosion earlier?

354
00:27:17.260 --> 00:27:18.200
Uh-huh.

355
00:27:19.540 --> 00:27:21.860
It was a bit of a tragedy.

356
00:27:22.560 --> 00:27:26.240
That robot you loved
so much... I blew it up.

357
00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:28.230
What?

358
00:27:29.190 --> 00:27:30.220
How could you?

359
00:27:32.720 --> 00:27:34.780
I want you to understand
something.

360
00:27:35.670 --> 00:27:37.930
This mission is
very difficult for me.

361
00:27:38.280 --> 00:27:40.020
I'd rather not draw this out.

362
00:27:48.030 --> 00:27:49.070
What was that?

363
00:27:49.910 --> 00:27:51.150
What the hell is this?

364
00:27:51.230 --> 00:27:52.330
We've suffered enough!

365
00:27:56.010 --> 00:27:56.840
Huh?

366
00:28:02.070 --> 00:28:03.090
Huh?

367
00:28:09.660 --> 00:28:10.460
Phew!

368
00:28:20.170 --> 00:28:21.070
That is spicy!

369
00:28:25.090 --> 00:28:25.610
You're back, huh?

370
00:28:25.610 --> 00:28:29.970
So this must be...

371
00:28:30.920 --> 00:28:33.690
Guess you survived
the Zappy Barrier twice!

372
00:28:33.770 --> 00:28:35.860
Man, you threw me
into that thing fast!

373
00:28:35.940 --> 00:28:37.640
Anyone smell burnt rubber?
